# proto-file: intrinsic/world/public/proto/object_world_updates.proto
# proto-message: intrinsic_proto.world.ObjectWorldUpdates

# The Prusa Core One (models/printer) on the ground in front of the reBot,
# its front (printer +Y: bezels, dial) facing the robot (yaw +90 deg about Z).
# The bed's top centre (heatbed.obj, printer (0.006, 0.030, 0.143)) lands at
# x=0.56, y=0, z=0.1434; the front bezels are at x=0.38. At this distance the
# 60 deg grasp (configs/rebot/app_config.yaml) reaches the bed's near and far
# edges, and from about 3 cm to either side the gripper meets the towers that
# flank the bed (offline check, step 3c).
updates {
  update_transform {
    node_a {
      by_name {
        object {
          object_name: "root"
        }
      }
    }
    node_b {
      by_name {
        object {
          object_name: "printer"
        }
      }
    }
    node_to_update {
      by_name {
        object {
          object_name: "printer"
        }
      }
    }
    a_t_b {
      position {
        x: 0.5895
        y: -0.0064
        z: 0
      }
      orientation {
        x: 0
        y: 0
        z: 0.70710678
        w: 0.70710678
      }
    }
  }
}
